('hikari-skin-massage', 'Hikari Skin Massage', '히카리 명동', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 명동8나길 18, 5층 502호 (충무로1가)', 'Skin & body massage (Japanese-friendly)', 'A long-running Myeongdong skin-and-body massage shop geared to Japanese-speaking visitors, near Myeongdong station.', 'It has served Myeongdong since around 2020 with Japanese-speaking staff and LINE booking — an easy, established choice for Japanese-speaking travellers.', 'skin and body massage in Myeongdong with Japanese-language service', 'Hikari is a skin-and-body massage shop on the fifth floor at 18 Myeongdong 8na-gil in Chungmuro 1-ga, near Myeongdong station exit 6. It has operated in Myeongdong since around 2020 and re-registered at this location, and is strongly oriented to Japanese-speaking visitors, with Japanese captions and LINE booking.

It books by LINE, phone and the heally platform. Services skew toward massage and skin/body care; English support is limited, so Japanese speakers will find it easiest.', null, null, null, 'https://www.instagram.com/hkr_massage', null, null, true),
('n-seoul-tower', 'N Seoul Tower', 'N 서울타워', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yongsan', '서울 용산구 남산공원길 105', 'Observation tower', 'Seoul''s landmark tower on Namsan — the city''s default first view, and its most photographed one after dark.', 'Nearly ten thousand ratings hold it at 4.2 — unusual consistency for a landmark that sees this much traffic, and a fair signal that the view delivers on the climb.', 'a first orientation to the city', 'N Seoul Tower stands at the summit of Namsan, in Yongsan-gu, and functions as the city''s orientation point: the observation deck gives you the whole basin at once, which is the fastest way to understand how Seoul is laid out before you start walking it.

The tower is busiest after sunset, when the night view is the draw. Its rating sits at 4.2 across more than 9,600 ratings — a large enough sample that the number means something. Getting up is part of the visit; the cable car from Myeongdong is the usual route, and the walk up through Namsan Park is the quieter one.

Namdaemun Market sits at the foot of the hill, close enough to pair the two in an afternoon.', 4.2, 9678, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=N%20Seoul%20Tower%20Yongsan%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/N%20%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8%ED%83%80%EC%9B%8C', true),
('lotte-world-tower-mall', 'Lotte World Tower & Mall', '롯데월드타워&몰', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jamsil', '서울 송파구 올림픽로 300(롯데월드 117~123층)', 'Skyscraper complex — mall, hotel & entertainment', 'Seoul''s tallest building — a 555-meter Jamsil complex holding a mall, hotel, and cinema, with the Seoul Sky observatory as just one part of it.', 'At 555 meters, it was among the world''s five tallest buildings when it opened in 2017 — worth knowing before deciding whether to also pay for the Seoul Sky ticket inside it.', 'a full afternoon of shopping and dining anchored by one landmark tower', 'Lotte World Tower & Mall is the 555-meter skyscraper complex that anchors Jamsil, in Songpa-gu — 123 floors that ranked among the world''s five tallest buildings on its 2017 opening. The tower holds the Signiel hotel and, on floors 117 to 123, the Seoul Sky observation deck, covered separately in this guide.

At street level the complex spreads into a shopping mall, a cinema, a concert hall, and a run of restaurants — enough to fill an afternoon before anyone goes near the observatory. Its rating sits at 4.4 across roughly 900 reviews, reflecting the mall and hotel experience as much as the tower itself.

It sits directly on Jamsil Station (lines 2 and 8), with the mall entrance built into the transit hub.', 4.4, 902, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lotte%20World%20Tower%20%26%20Mall%20Jamsil%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A1%AF%EB%8D%B0%EC%9B%94%EB%93%9C%ED%83%80%EC%9B%8C%26%EB%AA%B0', true),
('seoul-sky', 'Seoul Sky', '서울스카이', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jamsil', '서울 송파구 올림픽로 300(롯데월드타워 117~123층)', 'Observation deck', 'The observation deck on floors 117–123 of Lotte World Tower — the highest vantage point in Seoul, with a glass floor underfoot.', 'It''s the specific reason to go up the tower — the glass-floor section and the open-air Sky Terrace exist only at this level, separate from anything the mall below offers.', 'the highest view over Seoul, glass floor included', 'Seoul Sky occupies the top seven floors of Lotte World Tower — 117 through 123 — putting its observation floors between 472 and 498 meters above ground, the highest public vantage point in the city. The visit takes in a standard indoor observation floor, a glass-floored section that puts you directly over the drop, and an open-air Sky Terrace near the very top.

It shares its address and building with Lotte World Tower & Mall, but it is a separate, separately ticketed attraction — the tower''s shopping, dining, and hotel floors are a different visit, covered elsewhere in this guide. Seoul Sky holds a 4.3 rating across roughly 300 reviews.

Tickets are sold at a dedicated entrance inside the mall in Jamsil, and the elevator ride up is part of the experience.', 4.3, 303, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Seoul%20Sky%20Jamsil%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8%EC%8A%A4%EC%B9%B4%EC%9D%B4', true),
('seoul-city-wall', 'Seoul City Wall', '서울 한양도성', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 일대(단일 주소 없음)', 'Historic fortress wall / walking trail', 'Hanyangdoseong, the 18.6-kilometer Joseon-era fortress wall that still traces four of Seoul''s inner mountains — a walking route as much as a monument.', 'It''s on UNESCO''s tentative World Heritage list, and unlike most fortress walls this old, long stretches of it are still open to walk rather than roped off.', 'a self-guided heritage walk with skyline views built into the route', 'Seoul City Wall — Hanyangdoseong — was first built in 1396 to enclose the new Joseon capital and runs 18.6 kilometers along the ridgelines of Baegaksan, Naksan, Namsan, and Inwangsan. Rather than one site, it''s a network of walking courses: the Baegak course (Changuimun to Hyehwamun) and the Naksan course (Hyehwamun to Heunginjimun) are the two most associated with Jongno-gu, passing the Hanyangdoseong Museum and Naksan Park.

The wall links Seoul''s historic great and minor gates, and stretches along Naksan and Namsan open onto unobstructed views back over the city center — the Namsan course leads directly toward N Seoul Tower. It''s on UNESCO''s tentative World Heritage list.

There''s no single entrance; access is trailhead by trailhead, and the city''s official Hanyangdoseong site maps every course and gate.', 4.4, 195, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Seoul%20City%20Wall%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8%20%ED%95%9C%EC%96%91%EB%8F%84%EC%84%B1', true),
('jeongdong-observatory', 'Jeongdong Observatory', '정동전망대', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jeongdong', '서울 중구 덕수궁길 15 서울시청 서소문별관 13층', 'Free observation floor & café', 'A free public viewpoint on the 13th floor of Seoul City Hall''s Seosomun annex, looking straight down over Deoksugung Palace.', 'It holds a 4.4 average across a modest 37 ratings — a small but consistent number for a spot many visitors don''t know to look for.', 'a free, quiet view over Deoksugung without a ticket or a queue', 'Jeongdong Observatory sits on the 13th floor of Seoul City Hall''s Seosomun annex building in Jung-gu, looking directly down over Deoksugung Palace and the Jeongdong neighborhood around it. It opened in 2013, closed for a period afterward, and has since reopened with expanded hours: weekdays 13:30–17:30 and weekends 9:00–17:30, closed on most public holidays. Admission is free, and there''s a small café on the same floor.

As of mid-2026, Seoul City Hall also runs a second, newer observation floor in its main building nearby — a separate facility with its own entrance, not to be confused with this one. Both are free and city-run, but Jeongdong Observatory is the older, quieter of the two, and the one with the Deoksugung view.', 4.4, 37, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Jeongdong%20Observatory%20Jeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%A0%95%EB%8F%99%EC%A0%84%EB%A7%9D%EB%8C%80', true),
('gimpo-intl-airport-observatory-deck', 'Gimpo Int''l Airport Observatory Deck', '김포공항 전망대', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangseo', '서울 강서구 하늘길 78 김포국제공항', 'Outdoor airport observation deck', 'An outdoor deck on the domestic terminal''s 4th floor at Gimpo International Airport, close enough to watch aircraft taxi and take off.', null, 'watching domestic flights up close before or after a trip', 'Gimpo International Airport''s observatory deck sits at the far end of the 4th floor of the domestic passenger terminal, reachable straight from the terminal''s food court. It opened in October 2018 as part of the domestic terminal''s remodeling, and it''s an open-air deck separated from the apron by wire fencing rather than glass — close enough to watch aircraft push back, taxi, and take off.

Because it sits on the domestic side, only domestic flights are visible; the international terminal is on the opposite side of the airport grounds and out of view from here. The rating is modest, 3.5 across 20 ratings, in keeping with a bare-bones facility rather than a dedicated attraction — a free bonus for travelers already at the airport more than a destination on its own.

A different, no-longer-public viewing room elsewhere in the airport complex has a similar history; this is the domestic-terminal deck, still open to anyone passing through.', 3.5, 20, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gimpo%20Int''l%20Airport%20Observatory%20Deck%20Gangseo%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B9%80%ED%8F%AC%EA%B3%B5%ED%95%AD%20%EC%A0%84%EB%A7%9D%EB%8C%80', true),
('cultural-complex-j-bug', 'Cultural Complex J-Bug', '뚝섬 전망문화콤플렉스 J-Bug', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gwangjin', '서울 광진구 뚝섬한강공원 내(정식명칭 서울생각마루)', 'Riverside cultural complex — library, café & exhibits', 'A caterpillar-shaped cultural complex inside Ttukseom Hangang Park — officially Seoul Saenggak-maru — with a library, café, and river-facing views.', 'The building itself is the hook — a 243-meter structure shaped like an inchworm, which is where the nickname "J-Bug" comes from.', 'a quiet library-and-river break inside Ttukseom Hangang Park', 'Cultural Complex J-Bug is the popular nickname for Seoul Saenggak-maru, a 243-meter, caterpillar-shaped building inside Ttukseom Hangang Park in Gwangjin-gu. Inside are a public library, meeting rooms, a café, and a small exhibition hall on the Han River''s history — a low-key alternative to the park''s open lawns when the weather doesn''t cooperate.

Upper floors and the building''s river-facing side give views up and down the Han, though the site is built for lingering rather than for the view alone. It''s closed on Mondays and on New Year''s Day, Lunar New Year, and Chuseok.

The nearest access point is Jayang Station (Line 7), Ttukseom Hangang Park exit, about a ten-minute walk into the park.', 4, 9, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cultural%20Complex%20J-Bug%20Gwangjin%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%9A%9D%EC%84%AC%20%EC%A0%84%EB%A7%9D%EB%AC%B8%ED%99%94%EC%BD%A4%ED%94%8C%EB%A0%89%EC%8A%A4%20J-Bug', true),
('63-skypicnic', '63 Skypicnic', '63 스카이피크닉', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yeouido', '서울 영등포구 63로 50 63빌딩 내(비공식)', 'Art-and-media observation deck', 'A newly reopened art-and-media observatory on the 60th and 63rd floors of Yeouido''s 63 Building.', 'The 63rd-floor rooftop had been closed to visitors for years over safety concerns; its reopening as part of 63 Skypicnic in June 2026 is the news here.', 'a media-art take on the classic high-rise view, plus a rooftop rarely open to the public', '63 Skypicnic is the observation deck that opened inside Yeouido''s 63 Building on June 4, 2026, replacing the tower''s earlier observatory. The main level, on the 60th floor, combines a media-art installation with mirrored surfaces and projection screens, an immersive screening room, a café, and a gift shop rather than a plain viewing platform.

The draw beyond the art is the 63rd-floor rooftop, which reopened here after years of closure over safety concerns — one of the few genuinely open-air rooftops among Seoul''s tall-building observatories, and the best of the three levels for watching the Han River move from sunset into night.

Tickets are sold from the ground floor, with the observatory itself starting at the 60th.', 5, 10, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=63%20Skypicnic%20Yeouido%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/63%20%EC%8A%A4%EC%B9%B4%EC%9D%B4%ED%94%BC%ED%81%AC%EB%8B%89', true),
('riverview-8th-avenue', 'Riverview 8th Avenue', '광진교8번가', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangdong', '서울 강동구 선사로 4 광진교 중앙지점 하단', 'Bridge-pier river observatory', 'A glass-floored viewing platform built into a pier of Gwangjin Bridge — one of only three bridge-pier observatories in the world.', 'It''s one of only three observatories of its kind anywhere, alongside comparable decks on Paris''s Bir-Hakeim Bridge and Tokyo''s Rainbow Bridge — and visitor numbers back its growing reputation: the city''s own count went from roughly 15,000 in 2023 to over 107,000 in 2025.', 'a free, glass-floor view of the Han River built into a bridge pier', 'Riverview 8th Avenue sits beneath the eighth pier of Gwangjin Bridge, on the Gangdong-gu bank of the Han River. A glass floor lets visitors look straight down at the water, and the enclosed, glass-walled space frames both directions of the river along with the skylines of Gwangjin-gu and Gangdong-gu. It''s one of only three bridge-pier observatories in the world.

The space also hosts small exhibitions and occasional talks. It''s a seasonal facility, open only March through November and closed entirely from December through February; hours run noon to 6 p.m. in March and November and noon to 8 p.m. from April through October, and it''s also closed on Mondays, Lunar New Year, and Chuseok. Admission is free.

It''s about a 15-minute walk from either Gwangnaru or Cheonho station on Line 5.', 3.9, 9, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Riverview%208th%20Avenue%20Gangdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B4%91%EC%A7%84%EA%B5%908%EB%B2%88%EA%B0%80', true),
('chaeseokjang-observatory', 'Chaeseokjang Observatory', '채석장 전망대', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 낙산5길 51', 'Rooftop viewpoint & café', 'A rooftop viewpoint built atop a former Japanese colonial-era quarry cliff in Changsin-dong, with a café built into the level below.', 'The quarry it sits on supplied granite for colonial-era landmark buildings — a piece of Seoul''s history most skyline views don''t come with.', 'an off-the-tourist-track skyline view with real neighborhood history behind it', 'Chaeseokjang Observatory — also known as the Changsin-Sungin Quarry Observatory — sits atop a former granite quarry cliff in Changsin-dong, Jongno-gu. The quarry was cut into Naksan''s hillside during the Japanese colonial period to supply stone for buildings including the old Government-General building and the Bank of Korea; after the war, displaced families settled the quarry site into the hillside village that still surrounds the observatory today.

The building opened in 2019: a glass-walled second floor holds Café Nakta, and the rooftop above it is an open, unobstructed platform over the quarry cliff and the Seoul skyline beyond. It''s closed on Mondays.

It''s about an 11-minute walk from Changsin Station (Line 6), inside the same hillside neighborhood as Naksan Park.', null, 2, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chaeseokjang%20Observatory%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%B1%84%EC%84%9D%EC%9E%A5%20%EC%A0%84%EB%A7%9D%EB%8C%80', true),
('eungbongsan-palgakjeong', 'Eungbongsan Palgakjeong', '응봉산팔각정', 'observatory'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Seongdong', '서울 성동구 독서당로 362', 'Hilltop pavilion viewpoint', 'A traditional octagonal pavilion at the summit of Eungbongsan — one of Seoul''s classic Han River night-view spots, reached by a short hike.', 'The mountain served as a royal hunting ground in the Joseon dynasty, and the eight-sided pavilion at its summit is a small, quiet payoff for what''s only about a 30-minute climb.', 'a short hike to one of Seoul''s classic night-view spots', 'Eungbongsan Palgakjeong is the octagonal pavilion at the 94-meter summit of Eungbongsan, in Seongdong-gu, near where the Han River meets Jungnangcheon stream. A wooden staircase path climbs from the base to the pavilion in around 30 minutes, passing benches and exercise equipment along the way; the mountain itself served as a royal hunting ground during the Joseon dynasty.

From the pavilion, the view takes in the Han River, Apgujeong across the water, and — on clear days — Lotte World Tower and the mountains beyond, which is what has made it one of Seoul''s regularly recommended night-view spots.

The nearest stop is Eungbong Station on the Gyeongui-Jungang Line, about a ten-minute walk to the trailhead.', 5, 2, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Eungbongsan%20Palgakjeong%20Seongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%9D%91%EB%B4%89%EC%82%B0%ED%8C%94%EA%B0%81%EC%A0%95', true),
('namdaemun-market', 'Namdaemun Market', '남대문시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 남대문시장4길 21', 'Traditional general market', 'Korea''s largest traditional market, next to Sungnyemun Gate — clothing, housewares, and ginseng across about 20,000 wholesale and retail shops.', 'The wholesale side keeps overnight hours — 11pm to 4am — when retailers from around the country come in to buy.', 'browsing Korea''s largest general market, from clothing to ginseng', 'Namdaemun Market sits just north of Sungnyemun Gate in Jung-gu, and carries roughly 600 years of history by the city''s own count. It''s Korea''s largest traditional market, with about 20,000 wholesale and retail shops spread across the site.

The market deals in general merchandise rather than one specialty: clothing, eyewear, kitchenware, toys, mountain and fishing gear, stationery, hats, carpets, flowers, and ginseng all have their own stall clusters, alongside an imported-goods section. Daytime hours vary from store to store, and the wholesale side trades overnight, from 11pm to 4am.

It''s a short walk from Myeongdong and from Namsan, making it easy to fold into a walk that also takes in N Seoul Tower.', 3.9, 2966, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Namdaemun%20Market%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%82%A8%EB%8C%80%EB%AC%B8%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('kwangjang-market', 'Kwangjang Market', '광장시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 창경궁로 88', 'Traditional market and food alley', 'Korea''s first permanent private market, opened in 1905 — a food alley of bindaetteok, mayak gimbap, and yukhoe, alongside a second-floor fabric wholesale trade.', 'It opened in 1905 as Korea''s first permanent, privately funded market, and its second-floor fabric wholesale section still runs over 100 meters of stalls.', 'trying market-stall bindaetteok, mayak gimbap, and yukhoe in one alley', 'Kwangjang Market opened in 1905 in Jongno-gu, built with private Korean capital at a time when most markets were temporary, days-long affairs — making it the country''s first market designed to operate every day, permanently. Its name comes from the two bridges, Gwanggyo and Janggyo, that once stood at either end of the site.

The market''s food alley sells mung bean pancakes (bindaetteok), soy-and-mustard-dressed mini rolls known as mayak gimbap, and raw beef tartare (yukhoe) from stalls packed close together, most open from early morning into the evening. A second-floor fabric wholesale market runs alongside it, with stalls selling bolts of cloth.

It''s reachable on foot from either Jongno 5-ga Station (Line 1) or Euljiro 4-ga Station (Lines 2 and 5).', 4.2, 2368, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kwangjang%20Market%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B4%91%EC%9E%A5%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('ssamzigil', 'Ssamzigil', '쌈지길', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 인사동길 44', 'Craft shopping complex', 'A four-floor craft-shopping complex in Insadong, built around a spiral ramp that lets you walk the whole building without stairs.', 'The spiral ramp was built so you can walk all four floors without a single staircase — the layout is as much the point as what''s sold inside it.', 'craft shopping and a hands-on workshop class in Insadong', 'Ssamzigil opened in 2004 on Insadong-gil in Jongno-gu, built around a continuous spiral ramp that winds up through four above-ground floors without a staircase anywhere in the building. More than 70 craft shops line the ramp, selling ceramics, jewelry, stationery, and other handmade goods.

The basement floor holds an experience workshop where visitors can book same-day classes in pottery painting, mother-of-pearl inlay, leatherwork, glasswork, or soap-making. A ground-floor courtyard hosts rotating performances and exhibitions, and a rooftop garden sits above the top floor.

Ssamzigil is a short walk from Anguk Station (Line 3, Exit 6), in the middle of the wider Insadong shopping street.', 3.9, 469, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ssamzigil%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8C%88%EC%A7%80%EA%B8%B8', true),
('noryangjin-fisheries-wholesale-market', 'Noryangjin Fisheries Wholesale Market', '노량진 수산물 도매시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Noryangjin', '서울 동작구 노들로 674', 'Wholesale fish market', 'Seoul''s largest wholesale fish market, run by Suhyup — buy from the tanks on the trading floor, then have it prepared at one of the restaurants upstairs.', 'Auctions start in the middle of the night — shellfish from around 1am, live fish from 3am — so the floor is already trading hours before most of the city is up.', 'picking your own live seafood on the trading floor and eating it upstairs', 'Noryangjin Fisheries Wholesale Market, in Dongjak-gu, is Seoul''s largest consumer-facing fish market, operated by Suhyup Noryangjin Fisheries Co. The trading floor works on a section-by-section schedule: shellfish auctions from about 1am, premium fresh fish from 1:30am, live fish from 3am, with retail sales continuing through the day.

You can buy raw fish, shellfish, or other seafood directly from a tank-front vendor on the ground floor, then carry it upstairs to one of the market''s restaurants to have it sliced and served, paying only a preparation fee. The market closes on Sundays, January 1st, and the Lunar New Year and Chuseok holidays.

It''s next to Noryangjin Station, on Lines 1 and 9.', 3.9, 930, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Noryangjin%20Fisheries%20Wholesale%20Market%20Noryangjin%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%85%B8%EB%9F%89%EC%A7%84%20%EC%88%98%EC%82%B0%EB%AC%BC%20%EB%8F%84%EB%A7%A4%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('majang-meat-market', 'Majang Meat Market', '마장 축산물시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Seongdong', '서울 성동구 마장로31길 40', 'Wholesale meat market', 'Korea''s largest meat wholesale market, in Seongdong-gu — around 1,500 stalls trading hanwoo and other cuts, many of which will grill what you buy on the spot.', 'It handles an estimated 60 to 70% of livestock distribution across the greater Seoul area, with around 2 million visitors passing through its roughly 1,500 stalls each year.', 'buying hanwoo beef at wholesale stalls and having it grilled on the spot', 'Majang Meat Market, sometimes called Majang-dong Livestock Market, is Korea''s largest meat wholesale market, with roughly 1,500 vendors trading in Seongdong-gu. Livestock is processed and distributed through the market on an hourly basis, and the district''s own count puts its share of livestock distribution across the greater Seoul area at 60 to 70%.

Hanwoo — Korean native-breed beef — is the market''s signature product, sold directly from wholesale butchers rather than a retail counter. Many stalls will sell you a cut and point you to an adjoining grill room to cook and eat it immediately. General hours run from 3am to 11pm, with the market closed on the first and third Sunday of each month.

It''s about a 10-minute walk from either Yongdu Station (Line 2) or Majang Station (Line 5).', 4.3, 111, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Majang%20Meat%20Market%20Seongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A7%88%EC%9E%A5%20%EC%B6%95%EC%82%B0%EB%AC%BC%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('jungbu-market', 'Jungbu Market', '중부시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Euljiro', '서울 중구 을지로36길 35', 'Dried seafood wholesale market', 'A wholesale dried-seafood market in Euljiro — laver, seaweed, anchovies, squid, and pollack, sold by the box and in smaller retail quantities.', null, 'stocking up on dried seafood and Korean pantry staples by the box', 'Jungbu Market, in Jung-gu''s Euljiro neighborhood, specializes in dried seafood: laver and other seaweed, dried anchovies, yellow corvina, squid, pollack, and filefish fillets, sold both wholesale and retail. Ginseng is also sold alongside the seafood at a number of stores.

The market keeps wholesale hours, opening as early as 3 or 4am and largely closing by late afternoon, with stores shut on Sundays.

It''s about a two-minute walk from Euljiro 4-ga Station, on Lines 2 and 5.', 4.2, 115, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Jungbu%20Market%20Euljiro%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%A4%91%EB%B6%80%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('mangwon-market', 'Mangwon Market', '망원시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Mangwon', '서울 마포구 포은로8길 14', 'Neighborhood market', 'A neighborhood market in Mapo-gu selling fruit, vegetables, seafood, and street-food snacks, close to both Mangnidan-gil and Hangang Park.', null, 'a produce-and-food-stall neighborhood market next to Mangnidan-gil', 'Mangwon Market is a neighborhood market in Mangwon-dong, Mapo-gu, selling fruit, vegetables, seafood, and manufactured goods, alongside stalls of prepared food — deep-fried and braised chicken, jokbal, and battered green chili peppers among them.

It sits close to both Mangnidan-gil and Hangang Park, which makes it easy to fold into a walk through either. Stores keep their own hours and days off, generally closing around 9pm.

It''s a short walk from Mangwon Station, on Line 6.', 4.3, 48, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mangwon%20Market%20Mangwon%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A7%9D%EC%9B%90%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('garak-market', 'Garak Market', '가락시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Songpa', '서울 송파구 양재대로 932', 'Wholesale agricultural and marine market', 'Korea''s first public wholesale market for produce and seafood when it opened in 1985, and now the country''s largest — fruit, vegetables, and fisheries products traded at wholesale in Songpa-gu.', 'Around 7,300 tons of goods move through the market on a normal trading day.', 'seeing the scale of Korea''s largest wholesale produce and seafood market', 'Garak Market opened in June 1985 in Songpa-gu as Korea''s first public wholesale market for agricultural and marine products, and is now the largest in the country, on a site of 542,920 square meters. It trades fruit, vegetables, and fisheries products.

Wholesale trading runs overnight — the floor is already working at 2am, when most of the city is asleep.

It''s beside Garak Market Station, on Lines 3 and 8.', 4.2, 46, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Garak%20Market%20Songpa%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B0%80%EB%9D%BD%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('seoul-folk-flea-market', 'Seoul Folk Flea Market', '서울풍물시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 동대문구 천호대로4길 21', 'Flea market and antiques hall', 'An indoor flea market in seven color-coded buildings in Dongdaemun-gu — antiques, secondhand clothing, and household curios across nearly 900 shops.', 'The market''s seven buildings are each color-coded to a shade of the rainbow — a system that makes an 894-shop complex easier to navigate than it sounds.', 'digging through antiques and secondhand goods in one indoor market', 'Seoul Folk Flea Market — officially Seoul Pungmul Market — relocated to its current site near Sinseol-dong, where it now occupies seven buildings, each assigned one color of the rainbow, holding around 894 shops. It was named a Seoul Future Heritage site in 2015.

The market deals mostly in secondhand and antique goods: old furniture, clocks, cameras, records, tools, and vintage clothing are its core categories, with one building given over largely to antiques and handicrafts. Shop hours run 10am to 7pm, with the market''s food court staying open until 10pm; the whole market closes on Tuesdays.

It''s a short walk from Sinseol-dong Station, Exit 9, on Lines 1 and 2.', 3.6, 71, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Seoul%20Folk%20Flea%20Market%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8%ED%92%8D%EB%AC%BC%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('dongmyo-flea-market', 'Dongmyo Flea Market', '동묘벼룩시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 숭인동(동묘앞역 3번 출구 인근)', 'Outdoor flea market', 'An open-air secondhand market along the stone walls of Dongmyo Park, where merchants have gathered since the 1980s — vintage clothing and shoes are its biggest category now.', 'In the market''s clothing piles, pieces commonly go for ₩1,000 to ₩5,000.', 'sorting through streetside racks of secondhand and vintage clothing', 'Dongmyo Flea Market runs along the stone walls of Dongmyo Park in Jongno-gu, where merchants began gathering to sell secondhand goods in the 1980s. It has since grown into one of Seoul''s largest flea markets, with about 600 stalls along the walls and the side streets near Dongmyo Station.

Antiques are the base trade — rotary dial phones and old television sets, film posters, rare books, wallets — though vintage clothing and shoes have become the biggest category. Food stalls sell bindaetteok and boiled duck eggs among the goods. Stalls open daily from about 10am to 6pm, with hours varying by store.

It''s about 60 meters from Exit 3 of Dongmyo Station, on Lines 1 and 6.', 4.2, 35, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dongmyo%20Flea%20Market%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%8F%99%EB%AC%98%EB%B2%BC%EB%A3%A9%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('mapo-agricultural-marine-products-market', 'Mapo Agricultural & Marine Products Market', '마포 농수산물 시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Sangam', '서울 마포구 월드컵로 235', 'Wholesale seafood and produce market', 'A two-story seafood and produce market near Seoul World Cup Stadium — shops on the ground floor, sashimi centers and restaurants upstairs.', null, 'buying fresh seafood near World Cup Stadium and having it prepared upstairs', 'Mapo Agricultural and Marine Products Market opened in 1998 near Seoul World Cup Stadium in Mapo-gu''s Seongsan-dong, and is managed and run by the Mapo-gu Facilities Management Corporation. It''s a two-story standalone building: the ground floor holds shops selling seafood, fruit, and vegetables, plus a supermarket, and the second floor is given over to sashimi centers and restaurants.

Seafood bought downstairs can be carried up to be sliced and served on the floor above. The market has its own parking lot.

It''s near World Cup Stadium Station, on Line 6.', 3.9, 11, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mapo%20Agricultural%20%26%20Marine%20Products%20Market%20Sangam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A7%88%ED%8F%AC%20%EB%86%8D%EC%88%98%EC%82%B0%EB%AC%BC%20%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('gongdeok-market', 'Gongdeok Market', '공덕시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gongdeok', '서울 마포구 만리재로 19', 'Neighborhood market and jokbal alley', 'A neighborhood market on Mallijae-ro in Mapo-gu, home to Jokbal Alley — a row of braised pig''s-trotter restaurants — and, next to it, a Jeon Alley of Korean savory pancakes.', 'Jokbal Alley formed around 30 years ago, after one restaurant''s success drew others to open nearby; many of its stores have now been in place for more than 30 years.', 'jokbal — braised pig''s trotters — in Gongdeok''s Jokbal Alley', 'Gongdeok Market is on Mallijae-ro in Mapo-gu, about 130 meters from Exit 5 of Gongdeok Station. Jokbal Alley, inside the market, is a row of restaurants serving jokbal — pork trotters braised in soy sauce and spices — usually with sundae (Korean blood sausage) and sundaeguk, the soup made from it. Next to it, Jeon Alley has eateries serving jeon, Korean savory pancakes, lined up on either side of the lane.

Gongdeok Station is served by Lines 5 and 6, the Gyeongui–Jungang Line, and the Airport Railroad.', 3.7, 9, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gongdeok%20Market%20Gongdeok%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B3%B5%EB%8D%95%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('jongno-3-ga-stalls-alley', 'Jongno 3-ga Stalls Alley', '종로3가 포장마차 골목', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '', 'Street food stall alley', 'A stretch of orange-tented pojangmacha food carts near Jongno 3-ga Station that sets up after dark — seafood, tteokbokki, and fried snacks eaten standing at plastic tables.', null, 'an evening of pojangmacha-style street food and drinks', 'Jongno 3-ga''s stalls alley is a stretch of pojangmacha — orange-tented street food carts — that sets up along the sidewalk near Exits 5 and 6 of Jongno 3-ga Station once the sun goes down.

Menus vary cart to cart but lean toward tteokbokki, sundae stir-fry, tempura, kimchi pancakes, and grilled or raw seafood, eaten standing or seated at plastic tables and stools set up on the pavement. Carts typically open in the early evening and stay open late into the night.

The alley doesn''t have a single street address — it''s an informal cluster of vendors rather than one building — but it''s easy to find by walking out of Jongno 3-ga Station (Lines 1, 3, and 5) toward Exits 5 or 6 after dark.', 4.1, 8, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Jongno%203-ga%20Stalls%20Alley%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%A2%85%EB%A1%9C3%EA%B0%80%20%ED%8F%AC%EC%9E%A5%EB%A7%88%EC%B0%A8%20%EA%B3%A8%EB%AA%A9', true),
('yeongdeungpo-market', 'Yeongdeungpo Market', '영등포중앙시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yeongdeungpo', '서울 영등포구 영등포로 225', 'Neighborhood market', 'An old neighborhood market in Yeongdeungpo-gu, with a lane of sundae (blood sausage) shops facing each other from both sides.', null, 'sundaeguk — blood sausage soup — in the market''s sundae alley', 'Yeongdeungpo Market has operated in Yeongdeungpo-gu since around the end of Japanese colonial rule. Around 600 merchants trade there across 311 shops and 388 street stalls, selling manufactured goods, groceries, produce and seafood, dried fish, meat, and clothing.

One lane of the market is a sundae alley, where shops selling sundae (Korean blood sausage) and sundaeguk (blood sausage soup) face each other from both sides — one of them has been trading since 1966. Sundae is boiled in the afternoon, so that''s the better half of the day to come if you want to take some away.

It''s next to Yeongdeungpo Market Station, Exit 3, on Line 5.', 3.4, 18, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yeongdeungpo%20Market%20Yeongdeungpo%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%98%81%EB%93%B1%ED%8F%AC%EC%A4%91%EC%95%99%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('shinheung-market', 'Shinheung Market', '신흥시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yongsan', '서울 용산구 신흥로 95-9', 'Covered market turned café district', 'A 1950s covered market in Haebangchon, at the foot of Namsan, now home to independent bookstores, vintage shops, and cafés under a new transparent roof.', 'The market''s aging arcade roof was torn out and replaced with a clear cover, so the covered alley now lets in daylight whatever the weather.', 'café-hopping through a converted 1950s market arcade in Haebangchon', 'Shinheung Market was established in 1953 in Haebangchon, on a slope at the foot of Namsan in Yongsan-gu. It operated for decades as a conventional neighborhood market before its old, aging arcade roof was removed and replaced with a transparent cover, letting daylight into the covered alley regardless of weather.

Independent businesses have moved into much of the market since — bookstores, vintage and secondhand shops, and small cafés now occupy space once held by grocery and household-goods vendors, alongside a few longer-running food stalls. The alley is narrow and sloped, with old signage still hanging over new storefronts.

It''s within walking distance of Noksapyeong Station, on Line 6.', 4.4, 5, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shinheung%20Market%20Yongsan%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8B%A0%ED%9D%A5%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('gongneungdong-goblin-market', 'Gongneungdong Goblin Market', '공릉동 도깨비시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Nowon', '서울 노원구 동일로180길 37', 'Neighborhood market', 'A neighborhood market in Nowon-gu at the end of the Gyeongchun Line Forest Trail, tracing back to vendors who gathered by the old Gyeongchun railway line.', 'Its name comes from the vendors'' habit of scattering at the sign of a crackdown and reassembling along the tracks — there and gone like a goblin.', 'a market stop at the end of a Gyeongchun Line Forest Trail walk', 'Gongneungdong Goblin Market traces back to street vendors who gathered near what''s now Hwarangdae Station after the Gyeongchun railway line opened on July 25, 1939. It''s a covered, arcade-style market today, selling meat and produce, groceries, and miscellaneous goods, with restaurants mixed in.

It sits at the end of the Gyeongchun Line Forest Trail, the walking-and-cycling path built on the old railway''s former route. Since around 2019, the market has developed alongside that trail into more of a destination stop.

It''s near Taereung Entrance Station, on Lines 6 and 7.', 4.3, 3, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gongneungdong%20Goblin%20Market%20Nowon%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B3%B5%EB%A6%89%EB%8F%99%20%EB%8F%84%EA%B9%A8%EB%B9%84%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('yeongcheon-market', 'Yeongcheon Market', '영천시장', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Seodaemun', '서울 서대문구 성산로 704', 'Neighborhood market', 'A covered market in Seodaemun-gu, by Dongnimmun (Independence Gate) — once one of Seoul''s largest wholesale rice-cake markets.', 'Kkwabaegi — twisted doughnuts — are enough of a fixture here that more than ten shops were selling them in the market in the 1970s.', 'a covered neighborhood market by Independence Gate', 'Yeongcheon Market formed in the 1960s near Dongnimmun (Independence Gate) in Seodaemun-gu, starting as a tteok (rice cake) alley near the old Seodaemun Prison, and for a stretch of its history was one of Seoul''s largest wholesale markets for rice cakes. It runs under an arcade roof today, selling kkwabaegi (twisted doughnuts), tteokbokki, meat, fish, vegetables, and fruit.

Its northern entrance faces Dongnimmun, and the market is next to Dongnimmun Station on Line 3. Seodaemun Station, on Line 5, is about 500 meters away by Exit 2.', 4.3, 4, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yeongcheon%20Market%20Seodaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%98%81%EC%B2%9C%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%A5', true),
('myeongdong-night-market', 'Myeongdong Night Market', 'Myeongdong Night Market', 'market'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 충무로2길 3', 'Evening street food corridor', 'Myeongdong''s nightly street-food corridor — stalls set up along Myeongdong-gil and its side streets each evening, running roughly from dusk to around midnight.', null, 'an evening of Myeongdong''s street food once the daytime shops close', 'Myeongdong Night Market is the name commonly given to the street-food scene that takes over Myeongdong-gil and its side streets each evening, once the neighborhood''s daytime fashion and cosmetics shops start winding down. Vendors typically begin setting up carts in the late afternoon.

Skewers of grilled meat, hotteok (a filled, pan-fried sweet pancake), tteokbokki, grilled and battered seafood, and baked cheese dishes are the mainstays, sold from carts concentrated within a few minutes'' walk of Myeongdong Station. Unlike Namdaemun or Gwangjang, it isn''t organized around a single market building — it''s an evening layer on top of Myeongdong''s regular shopping street, and it packs up again by around midnight.

It''s centered on Myeongdong Station, Exit 6, on Line 4.', 4.7, 18, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Myeongdong%20Night%20Market%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Myeongdong%20Night%20Market', true),
('starfield-coex-mall', 'Starfield COEX Mall', '스타필드 코엑스몰', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangnam', '서울 강남구 영동대로 513', 'Underground shopping mall', 'The underground mall beneath the COEX complex in Samseong-dong, holding an aquarium, a multiplex and a free public library.', 'It holds a 4.0 rating across more than 900 ratings — a large enough sample for the number to mean something.', 'a long indoor afternoon that mixes shopping with an aquarium and a library', 'Starfield COEX Mall runs beneath the COEX complex at 513 Yeongdong-daero, in Samseong-dong. Alongside the shops it holds the COEX Aquarium, a Megabox multiplex and the Starfield Library.

The library occupies two levels at the middle of the mall — 2,800 square metres, shelves thirteen metres high, around 70,000 books and some 600 magazine titles, open to anyone at no charge. Around it run the fashion, beauty and food-and-beverage floors, and the mall keeps one set of hours, 10:30 to 22:00.

You can reach all of it without going outside. Samseong Station on Line 2 connects directly through Exits 5 and 6 by way of Millennium Plaza, and Bongeunsa Station on Line 9 connects through Exit 7 by way of ASEM Plaza.', 4, 902, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Starfield%20COEX%20Mall%20Gangnam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8A%A4%ED%83%80%ED%95%84%EB%93%9C%20%EC%BD%94%EC%97%91%EC%8A%A4%EB%AA%B0', true),
('goto-mall', 'GOTO Mall', '고투 몰', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Seocho', '서울 서초구 신반포로 194', 'Underground shopping arcade', 'The 620-shop arcade under the Express Bus Terminal — the largest of the 25 underground arcades the city operates.', 'It is public infrastructure rather than a retail development — the Seoul Facilities Corporation runs it as one of 25 city-owned arcades, which is why the passageways stay open 24 hours whether or not the shops are.', 'shopping without going outside, between the subway and the bus terminal', 'GOTO Mall is the underground shopping arcade beneath the Express Bus Terminal in Seocho-gu, run by the Seoul Facilities Corporation as one of the 25 arcades the city owns. It covers 31,566 square metres and holds 620 shops, which makes it the largest of those 25 by both floor area and shop count.

The corporation lists its goods as clothing, flowers and household items, plus restaurants. Shops keep 10:00 to 22:00; the passageways themselves stay open 24 hours, so the arcade doubles as a route between the trains and the coaches.

Express Bus Terminal Station sits directly above it, served by Lines 3, 7 and 9, and the arcade links the station to the terminal building where buses leave for the rest of the country.', 4.1, 290, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=GOTO%20Mall%20Seocho%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B3%A0%ED%88%AC%20%EB%AA%B0', true),
('ipark-mall', 'I''Park Mall', '아이파크몰', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yongsan', '서울 용산구 한강대로23길 55', 'Station-attached shopping complex', 'The eleven-floor mall built into Yongsan Station — department store halls, an electronics centre, a cinema and an e-sports arena.', 'It is built into Yongsan Station rather than near it, so the shops are reachable straight from the concourse without going outside.', 'filling the hours before a train out of Yongsan Station', 'I''Park Mall stands at 55 Hangang-daero 23-gil and connects directly into Yongsan Station, which is the first thing to know about it — you reach the shops from the station without stepping outside.

Inside, it divides into the I''Park Department Store, itself split into Living, Culture and Fashion halls, plus a Digital Shopping Center and an Event Park. Alongside those are a CGV cinema, an e-sports stadium, an E-mart, a bookstore, a culture centre and more than a hundred restaurants, spread over eleven floors.

Hours run 10:30 to 20:30 Sunday through Thursday and 10:30 to 21:00 on Fridays and Saturdays, with floors one to three and the fashion park on four staying open to 22:00.', 3.9, 118, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=I''Park%20Mall%20Yongsan%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%95%84%EC%9D%B4%ED%8C%8C%ED%81%AC%EB%AA%B0', true),
('lotte-outlets-seoul-station', 'Lotte Outlets Seoul Station', '롯데아울렛 서울역점', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yongsan', '서울 중구 한강대로 405', 'Outlet mall', 'Three outlet floors inside the Seoul Station building, carrying 84 brands above a Lotte Mart.', 'It is inside the station building rather than beside it, and the Lotte Mart below it stays open to 23:00 — two hours after the outlet floors have closed.', 'a shopping stop worked into a departure from Seoul Station', 'Lotte Outlets Seoul Station takes up three floors of the Seoul Station building at 405 Hangang-daero, in Jung-gu. It carries 84 brands across about 3,400 pyeong — roughly 11,000 square metres — among them the first North Face outlet store, and there are paid lockers on site for anyone shopping between trains.

The outlet floors run 10:30 to 21:00. Sharing the same building beneath them is a Lotte Mart branded Zettaplex, open 10:00 to 23:00 and closed two Wednesdays a month, with immediate tax refunds available to foreign shoppers.', 3.6, 288, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lotte%20Outlets%20Seoul%20Station%20Yongsan%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A1%AF%EB%8D%B0%EC%95%84%EC%9A%B8%EB%A0%9B%20%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8%EC%97%AD%EC%A0%90', true),
('ifc-mall', 'IFC Mall', 'IFC 몰', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Yeouido', '서울 영등포구 국제금융로 10', 'Underground shopping mall', 'Three basement levels under the International Finance Centre towers on Yeouido, reached from the station by a 360-metre moving walkway.', null, 'a cinema and a bookshop in the middle of the office district', 'IFC Mall occupies three basement levels beneath the International Finance Centre at 10 Gukjegeumyung-ro, on Yeouido. It opened in 2012 and holds around 110 brands — fashion, beauty, sportswear and accessories — plus restaurants, a nine-screen CGV cinema and a Youngpoong Bookstore.

The approach is the distinctive part. A 360-metre moving walkway runs from Yeouido Station, where Lines 5 and 9 interchange, straight into the mall, so you never come up to street level.

Mall hours are 10:00 to 22:00; the street-level shops close an hour earlier, at 21:00.', 4, 188, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=IFC%20Mall%20Yeouido%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/IFC%20%EB%AA%B0', true),
('common-ground', 'Common Ground', '커먼그라운드', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gwangjin', '서울 광진구 아차산로 200', 'Container shopping complex', 'A complex assembled from 200 shipping containers outside Konkuk University, open since April 2015.', 'The containers aren''t a decorative theme — the whole structure is 200 of them, stacked into two facing blocks.', 'browsing a shopping complex built out of freight containers', 'Common Ground stands at 200 Achasan-ro in Gwangjin-gu, built from 200 shipping containers and open since 10 April 2015. The containers are stacked into two facing blocks, Street Market and Market Hall, and the complex''s other named zones are a Culture Space, a Terrace Market and a Market Ground.

Street Market holds thirty shops and Market Hall carries 26 boutique brands, with an Adidas Originals store occupying a zone of its own.

Opening hours are 11:00 to 22:00, with some of the third-floor food tenants running to 01:00 at weekends. Konkuk University Station, where Lines 2 and 7 meet, is Exit 3 and about three minutes away on foot.', 3.7, 186, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Common%20Ground%20Gwangjin%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%BB%A4%EB%A8%BC%EA%B7%B8%EB%9D%BC%EC%9A%B4%EB%93%9C', true),
('myeongdong-underground-shopping-center', 'Myeongdong Underground Shopping Center', '명동지하상가', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 남대문로지하 72', 'Underground shopping arcade', 'A 61-shop arcade under Namdaemun-ro listed for eyewear and clothing — and entered from Euljiro 1-ga Station, not Myeongdong Station.', 'The operator gives its main goods as eyeglasses and clothing, and the name misleads on access: the entrance is at Euljiro 1-ga, while the arcade under Myeongdong Station is a different one.', 'eyeglasses, and a covered route between Euljiro and Myeongdong', 'The Myeongdong Underground Shopping Center runs under Namdaemun-ro at basement number 72, one of the 25 underground arcades the Seoul Facilities Corporation operates. It covers 3,838 square metres and holds 61 shops; the operator lists its main goods as eyeglasses and clothing.

The name is misleading about how you get in. The arcade connects to Euljiro 1-ga Station on Line 2, at Exit 7 — not to Myeongdong Station. There is a separate arcade at Myeongdong Station on Line 4, running under Toegye-ro with 70 shops of its own selling clothing, bags and accessories.

Shops open 09:00 to 22:00 and the arcade trades year-round; the passageway itself stays open 24 hours.', 3.6, 65, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Myeongdong%20Underground%20Shopping%20Center%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%AA%85%EB%8F%99%EC%A7%80%ED%95%98%EC%83%81%EA%B0%80', true),
('apm-place', 'Apm Place', '에이피엠 플레이스', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 중구 을지로 276', 'Wholesale fashion building', 'A twelve-storey wholesale fashion building in Dongdaemun that trades overnight, from 8pm to 5am, and closes at weekends.', 'Its hours say what it is: 8pm to 5am, shut Friday and Saturday. This building runs on the buyers'' week, not the shopper''s weekend.', 'buying women''s clothing wholesale on Dongdaemun''s night schedule', 'apM PLACE is at 276 Euljiro, one of three apM buildings in Dongdaemun — with apM and apM Luxe — that trade as wholesale fashion malls.

The selling floors are given over almost entirely to women''s clothing, filling floors one through eight and the first basement, with miscellaneous goods on the second basement. Above the shop floors the building turns over to storage on nine, offices on ten, and officetels on eleven and twelve; parking sits on basement levels four and five.

Trading runs from 8:00pm to 5:00am the following morning, and the building is closed on Fridays and Saturdays. That is the Dongdaemun wholesale cycle rather than an ordinary mall''s timetable, so anyone arriving in the daytime will find the shutters down.', 3.9, 21, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Apm%20Place%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%97%90%EC%9D%B4%ED%94%BC%EC%97%A0%20%ED%94%8C%EB%A0%88%EC%9D%B4%EC%8A%A4', true),
('stylenanda-pink-hotel-flagship-store', 'Stylenanda Pink Hotel Flagship Store', '스타일난다 핑크호텔', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 명동8길 37-8', 'Brand flagship store', 'Stylenanda''s Myeongdong flagship — a store fitted out to look like a hotel, carrying the brand''s 3CE cosmetics line.', null, '3CE cosmetics bought at the brand''s own flagship', 'The Stylenanda Pink Hotel is the brand''s Myeongdong flagship, at 37-8 Myeongdong 8-gil in Jung-gu, and has been open since October 2016. Seoul''s official tourism listing describes it as a store fitted out to look like a hotel — the conceit its name refers to.

What it carries is the brand''s own range, including 3CE, the cosmetics line Nanda launched in 2004.

It opens at 12:00 and closes at 21:00. Myeongdong Station Exit 6, on Line 4, is 148 metres away.', 4.1, 71, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stylenanda%20Pink%20Hotel%20Flagship%20Store%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8A%A4%ED%83%80%EC%9D%BC%EB%82%9C%EB%8B%A4%20%ED%95%91%ED%81%AC%ED%98%B8%ED%85%94', true),
('mecenatpolis-mall', 'Mecenatpolis Mall', '메세나폴리스몰', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Hapjeong', '서울 마포구 양화로 45', 'Open-air street mall', 'An open-air street mall at the foot of the Mecenatpolis towers in Hapjeong, connected directly to the station.', 'A Lotte Cinema and a performance venue, the Lotte Card Art Center, are built into the same complex as the shops and the supermarket.', 'a cinema, a supermarket and a meal without an enclosed mall around them', 'Mecenatpolis Mall sits at 45 Yanghwa-ro in Seogyo-dong, at the base of the Mecenatpolis complex — three residential towers plus offices, completed in 2012. The Korea Tourism Organization classifies the mall itself as a street mall, meaning its shops line open walkways rather than enclosed corridors.

Tenants cover fashion and beauty, a large supermarket, and a run of restaurants and cafés. A Lotte Cinema is on site, as is the Lotte Card Art Center, a performance venue.

The mall connects directly to Hapjeong Station, where Lines 2 and 6 interchange.', 3.9, 80, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mecenatpolis%20Mall%20Hapjeong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A9%94%EC%84%B8%EB%82%98%ED%8F%B4%EB%A6%AC%EC%8A%A4%EB%AA%B0', true),
('garden-5', 'Garden 5', '가든파이브', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Songpa', '서울 송파구 충민로 66', 'Suburban shopping complex', 'A four-hall retail complex at Jangji Station, built by the city to rehouse traders displaced by the Cheonggyecheon restoration.', 'Roughly 4,000 retail units sit across its four halls, anchored by an NC Department Store, a Hyundai City Mall outlet and a CGV multiplex.', 'a full-day mall trip in southeastern Seoul', 'Garden 5 is at 66 Chungmin-ro in Munjeong-dong, in southeastern Seoul. Songpa-gu''s own listing describes four halls — Fashion, Main, Living and Techno — holding roughly 4,000 retail units between them.

The complex exists because of the Cheonggyecheon restoration. Seoul''s city government, through its SH Corporation, developed it as somewhere the traders cleared from the stream''s banks could reopen, and it opened in June 2010.

The large tenants today are an NC Department Store, a Hyundai City Mall urban outlet and a CGV multiplex. Hours are 10:30 to 21:00 Monday to Thursday and 10:30 to 22:00 Friday to Sunday, with the food halls running 10:00 to 23:00 every day. Jangji Station on Line 8 is Exit 4.', 3.8, 31, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Garden%205%20Songpa%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B0%80%EB%93%A0%ED%8C%8C%EC%9D%B4%EB%B8%8C', true),
('nampyeonghwa-sangga', 'Nampyeonghwa Sangga', '남평화 상가', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 중구 장충단로 282-10', 'Wholesale bag & clothing market', 'A wholesale market for bags and clothing on the Dongdaemun edge of Jung-gu, trading since 1980 across a basement and three floors.', 'Bags are the specialism rather than a side line: the basement and the whole ground floor are given to them, in a building that has been trading since 1980.', 'bags bought wholesale, on the market''s own hours', 'Nampyeonghwa Sangga is a wholesale market for bags and clothing at 282-10 Jangchungdan-ro, in Sindang-dong on the Dongdaemun side of Jung-gu. It has been trading since 1980 and holds around 700 shops across a basement and three floors.

Stock is arranged by level: bags in the basement and on the ground floor, young casual wear on the second floor, denim and women''s clothing on the third.

The hours split the same way. The basement and ground floor trade from midnight to noon; the second and third floors trade from 8:00pm to 5:00am. The whole building is closed on Fridays and Saturdays, and on the days it does open, no floor trades in the afternoon.', 3.8, 35, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nampyeonghwa%20Sangga%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%82%A8%ED%8F%89%ED%99%94%20%EC%83%81%EA%B0%80', true),
('hello-apm', 'Hello APM', '헬로에이피엠', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 중구 장충단로 253', 'Retail fashion building', 'A Dongdaemun fashion building that trades retail rather than wholesale, with the clothing on its lower four floors — open to 1am, closed Tuesdays.', 'Only part of the building is a mall. Clothing occupies the basement and floors one to four; five to seven are listed as vacant, and everything above is a gym, clinics and offices.', 'late-evening clothes shopping in Dongdaemun without wholesale hours', 'Hello apm is at 253 Jangchungdan-ro in Dongdaemun. The Dongdaemun Fashion Town tourist-zone directory lists it as a shopping centre and discount store rather than a wholesale building, and the hours match: 10:20 in the morning until 1:00am, closed on Tuesdays.

Clothing sits on the lower floors — women''s wear on one, two and three, with women''s accessories on three; children''s wear and wedding goods, including hanbok, bedding, jewellery and curtains, also on two; men''s wear and accessories on four. The basement carries shoes, imported cosmetics, tourist goods and a comics café, and there is a pharmacy on the ground floor.

Floors five to seven are listed as vacant. The floors above them are not retail at all: a gym on eight, screen golf and billiards on nine, dental, paediatric, obstetric and dermatology clinics on ten, and management offices on eleven.', 3.3, 32, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hello%20APM%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%ED%97%AC%EB%A1%9C%EC%97%90%EC%9D%B4%ED%94%BC%EC%97%A0', true),
('myeongdong-migliore', 'Myeongdong Migliore', '명동밀리오레', 'mall'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 퇴계로 115', 'Fashion & lifestyle arcade', 'Two retail floors at Myeongdong Station Exit 6, under fifteen storeys of hotel — remodelled and reopened in August 2024.', 'It sits directly at Myeongdong Station Exit 6, and what''s on its two floors is a mix rather than a category — an Olive Young, a handful of fashion labels, a K-pop merchandise shop and cafés.', 'a short stop right outside Myeongdong Station Exit 6', 'Myeongdong Migliore is at 115 Toegye-ro, directly in front of Myeongdong Station Exit 6. Migliore opened its first branch in Dongdaemun in February 1998 and this Myeongdong branch in 2000.

The building now does two jobs at once. Floors one and two are the shopping mall; floors three to seventeen operate as a hotel. The two retail floors were remodelled and reopened in August 2024.

What''s on them is a mix rather than one category: Olive Young and Giordano, fashion labels including Folder, Roem, Drawfit and Instant Punk, the K-pop merchandise shop AllThatKpop, and cafés. Opening hours are set store by store rather than for the building, so each shop keeps its own.

Its rating stands at 3.1 across 42 ratings — a small sample.', 3.1, 42, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Myeongdong%20Migliore%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%AA%85%EB%8F%99%EB%B0%80%EB%A6%AC%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%88', true),
('spa-gogyeol', 'Spa Gogyeol', '스파고결', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangnam', '서울 강남구 선릉로132길 13 J&C빌딩 4층', 'Manual therapy spa', 'Cheongdam treatment spa worked entirely by hand, with a second branch in Seocho.', null, 'a hands-only Korean manual therapy session', 'Spa Gogyeol is at 13 Seolleung-ro 132-gil in Cheongdam, a private treatment spa rather than a bathhouse. The description it gives of its own work is a narrow one: care worked entirely by the therapist''s hands, in the Korean sugi manual-therapy tradition, read from each client''s skin and muscle rather than run off a fixed course.

The business runs two branches — this one and a second in Seocho, at 42 Seocho-jungang-ro. Booking for either goes through Naver, KakaoTalk or Instagram rather than one central page. The Cheongdam address is a fourth-floor unit.', 5, 269, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Spa%20Gogyeol%20Gangnam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%EA%B3%A0%EA%B2%B0', true),
('laurel-studio', 'Laurel Studio', 'Laurel studio', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Hongdae', '서울 마포구 월드컵북로 7, 3층', 'K-beauty facial studio', 'K-beauty facial studio in Hongdae where the treatment is taken lying on a traditional ondol floor, from therapists in hanbok.', 'There is no treatment bed. You lie on a traditional ondol floor, and the therapists work in remade hanbok.', 'an ondol-floor facial in Hongdae', 'Laurel Studio is on the third floor at 7 World Cup-buk-ro, in Mapo-gu, about 250 metres from Exit 1 of Hongik University Station.

What sets the treatment apart is where it happens: rather than a treatment bed, you lie on a traditional ondol floor, and the therapists work in remade hanbok. Every session opens with a skin checklist, and the treatment is set from what it finds.

There are two programmes — a basic facial of about 50 minutes, and a premium version of about 60 that adds a skincare routine written for you and sent on afterwards. A session takes up to four people. The studio was founded by a former cosmetics ingredient researcher.

Booking is by WhatsApp or Instagram message, or through the studio''s own booking page. English is available, and the studio provides foreign-language guide cards by country. Published opening hours differ between listings, so confirm your slot when you book.', 5, 21, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Laurel%20studio%20Hongdae%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Laurel%20studio', true),
('dolce-far-niente', 'Dolce Far Niente', '달콤한 게으름', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gongdeok', '서울 마포구 만리재로 93, 2층', 'Skincare & spa treatments', 'Skincare and spa room listed on the second floor at 93 Manrijae-ro in Mapo-gu.', null, 'confirming what is offered before booking', 'Dolce Far Niente is listed as a spa on the second floor at 93 Manrijae-ro, in Mapo-gu, a short way from Gongdeok.

Beyond the name and the address we found nothing published about it in Korean or English: no operator page, no social account, no treatment menu, no price list and no opening hours. With no way to establish what the business offers, the entry stays unverified and is not published in the directory.', 5, 12, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dolce%20Far%20Niente%20Gongdeok%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%8B%AC%EC%BD%A4%ED%95%9C%20%EA%B2%8C%EC%9C%BC%EB%A6%84', false),
('aroma-thai-spa-gongdeok', 'Aroma Thai Spa Gongdeok', '아로마 타이 스파 공덕점', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gongdeok', '서울 마포구 독막로 320 태영 데시앙101동 지하 101호', 'Thai spa', 'Thai spa in a basement unit of the Taeyoung Desian complex, in Mapo-gu''s Gongdeok area.', null, 'a Thai spa appointment in the Gongdeok area', 'Aroma Thai Spa occupies unit B101, a basement space in the Taeyoung Desian complex at 320 Dokmak-ro in Mapo-gu, in the Gongdeok area.

It is listed as a Thai spa, and that is as far as the published record goes — no treatment menu, no price list, and no operator site we could open. A phone number is listed, which is the practical way in.

Published opening hours differ between listings, so confirm the closing time before you plan around it.', 4.9, 336, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Aroma%20Thai%20Spa%20Gongdeok%20Gongdeok%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%95%84%EB%A1%9C%EB%A7%88%20%ED%83%80%EC%9D%B4%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%20%EA%B3%B5%EB%8D%95%EC%A0%90', true),
('lavish-spa', 'Lavish Spa', '레비쉬 스파', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 동숭3길 6-4, 2층', 'Massage studio', 'Second-floor massage studio on Dongsung 3-gil in Jongno.', null, 'a massage in Jongno''s Dongsung-dong', 'Lavish Spa is a massage studio on the second floor at 6-4 Dongsung 3-gil, in Jongno-gu.

It publishes a phone number and an Instagram account, @lavishspa, and little else — no treatment menu, no price list, no site of its own. That makes it a place to call before you go rather than one to plan a day around. Ask what a course covers and confirm the hours; neither is published anywhere we could check.', 4.9, 98, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lavish%20Spa%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A0%88%EB%B9%84%EC%89%AC%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C', true),
('2s-apgujeong', '2s Apgujeong', '2s 압구정', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Apgujeong', '서울 강남구 선릉로157길 6, 4층', 'Spa', 'Listed as a spa on Seolleung-ro 157-gil in Apgujeong, with almost nothing published about it.', null, 'confirming what is offered before booking', '2s is listed as a spa on the fourth floor at 6 Seolleung-ro 157-gil, in Apgujeong.

We could not find anything published about it beyond that address — no operator page, no treatment menu, no tourism or trade listing. The entry stays unverified on that basis, and is not published in the directory. Confirm what is offered, and at what price, before booking.', 4.9, 16, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=2s%20Apgujeong%20Apgujeong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/2s%20%EC%95%95%EA%B5%AC%EC%A0%95', false),
('marzia-healing-spa-cheongdam', 'Marzia Healing Spa - Cheongdam', '마르지아 힐링 스파 - 청담', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Cheongdam', '', 'Day spa', 'Cheongdam day spa working by appointment, with a programme range from facials to scalp and men''s care.', null, 'a booked day-spa course in Cheongdam', 'Marzia Healing Spa''s Cheongdam branch is a day spa that works by appointment rather than walk-in.

The programme range covers facial care, body care, scalp care and a separate men''s line, plus sugaring hair removal, and courses built around particular circumstances — wedding preparation, pregnancy, and treatments for children. Korea''s national tourism organisation describes the approach as traditional Korean practice combined with European aromatherapy technique.

We are not listing an address for this branch. Two official listings give different ones and we could not confirm either as current, so ask for the address when you book, and confirm the course at the same time.', 4.9, 14, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marzia%20Healing%20Spa%20-%20Cheongdam%20Cheongdam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%A7%88%EB%A5%B4%EC%A7%80%EC%95%84%20%ED%9E%90%EB%A7%81%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%20-%20%EC%B2%AD%EB%8B%B4', true),
('stone-house-head-spa', 'Stone House Head Spa', '스톤 하우스 헤드 스파', 'head_spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangnam', '서울 강남구 언주로147길 B63-22 B1, A동', 'Head spa', 'Head spa listed on a basement level off Eonju-ro 147-gil in Gangnam, with nothing published about it.', null, 'confirming what is offered before booking', 'Stone House Head Spa is listed at Eonju-ro 147-gil B63-22, basement level of building A, in Gangnam-gu.

We found nothing published about it in Korean or English — no operator page, no social account, no treatment menu or price list, and no business listing that matches. The address as we hold it does not resolve to a standard road-name address either, which may be part of the reason.

With no way to establish what the business offers, the entry stays unverified and is not published in the directory.', 4.9, 11, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stone%20House%20Head%20Spa%20Gangnam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8A%A4%ED%86%A4%20%ED%95%98%EC%9A%B0%EC%8A%A4%20%ED%97%A4%EB%93%9C%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C', false),
('create-wellness-center', 'Create Wellness Center', '크레이트 웰네스', 'wellness'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Itaewon', '서울 용산구 이태원로 211 한남빌딩 1층', 'Chiropractic & rehabilitation clinic', 'Chiropractic and rehabilitation clinic on Itaewon-ro, working in English since 2001.', 'It is a clinic rather than a treatment room: chiropractic, rehabilitation, therapeutic massage, naturopathy and osteopathy under one roof, in English as well as Korean.', 'English-language treatment for back, neck or joint pain', 'Create Wellness Center is on the ground floor of the Hannam Building at 211 Itaewon-ro, in Yongsan-gu, near Exit 2 of Itaewon Station.

It is a clinic rather than a gym or a spa. The work is US chiropractic, rehabilitation, therapeutic massage, visceral osteopathy, naturopathy and nutritional consultation, with mat pilates run as group exercise alongside. The centre has worked with Korea''s foreign community since 2001, with internationally trained practitioners and bilingual staff, and it runs a second branch on Jeju.

Hours are 09:00 to 19:00 on weekdays and 09:00 to 18:00 at weekends, with the clinic closed between 13:00 and 14:00. Appointments go through the Mindbody app, by phone or email, or by message on Instagram or Facebook.', 4.8, 30, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Create%20Wellness%20Center%20Itaewon%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%ED%81%AC%EB%A0%88%EC%9D%B4%ED%8A%B8%20%EC%9B%B0%EB%84%A4%EC%8A%A4', true),
('eco-jardin-aeogae-branch', 'Eco Jardin (Aeogae)', 'Eco Jardin Aeogae Branch', 'head_spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gongdeok', '서울 마포구 마포대로 204, 2층', 'Head spa & hair salon', 'The Eco Jardin group''s Aeogae branch — a hair salon whose head spa runs to a published fifteen- or eighteen-step scalp programme.', 'The scalp programme is published step by step, and the scalp is read under a microscope at the start and again near the end — so the before and after is something you look at.', 'a step-by-step scalp treatment near Aeogae Station', 'This is the Aeogae branch of Eco Jardin, on the second floor of the Mapo SK Hub Blue building at 204 Mapo-daero, in Ahyeon-dong, Mapo-gu. It is not the group''s Jongno branch, a separate premises at 9 Jahamun-ro near Gyeongbokgung, nor the Jamsil one; Eco Jardin runs several salons in Seoul and franchises the name.

The branch is registered as a beauty business, was established in February 2024 and takes four units on its floor. It carries the group''s main Instagram account, which names it the Aeogae flagship, and bookings are taken by direct message or WhatsApp rather than by phone.

The head spa here comes in two lengths. Both open with a microscope reading of the scalp and take a second one three steps from the end; between them run neck work and suction, a hot towel, an aroma-oil cleanse and a scrub, steam, shampoo, and tonic and stick treatments. The eighteen-step version adds a scalp massage, a herbal pack and a steam cap to the fifteen.', 4.8, 17, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Eco%20Jardin%20Aeogae%20Branch%20Gongdeok%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Eco%20Jardin%20Aeogae%20Branch', true),
('provence-spa-by-loccitane', 'Provence Spa by L''OCCITANE', '프로방스 스파 바이 록시땅', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 종로구 청계천로 279 JW 메리어트 동대문 스퀘어 서울 9층', 'Hotel spa', 'L''OCCITANE''s spa inside the JW Marriott Dongdaemun Square, bookable whether or not you are staying.', 'The hotel opens it to non-residents, so the spa is bookable on its own — you do not have to be a guest to use it.', 'a French-brand facial and body course in Dongdaemun', 'Provence Spa is the L''OCCITANE-branded spa inside the JW Marriott Dongdaemun Square Seoul, at 279 Cheonggyecheon-ro in Jongno-gu.

It works with the French brand''s own oils and plant extracts. The menu covers facials, hair and scalp treatments, body scrubs, wraps and massages, with couples'' treatments as an option. The signature course, the Immortelle Divine Journey to Perfection, pairs an anti-ageing facial with shoulder, back and foot massage, using organic immortelle and myrtle.

Both hotel guests and non-residents can book. The hotel''s other wellness facilities — a 25-metre indoor lap pool and the Club 501 fitness centre — are separate from the spa.', 4.8, 13, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Provence%20Spa%20by%20L''OCCITANE%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%ED%94%84%EB%A1%9C%EB%B0%A9%EC%8A%A4%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%20%EB%B0%94%EC%9D%B4%20%EB%A1%9D%EC%8B%9C%EB%95%85', true),
('the-spa-grand-hyatt-seoul', 'The Spa Grand Hyatt Seoul', '더 스파 그랜드 하얏트 서울', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Itaewon', '서울 용산구 소월로 322 Garden Level', 'Hotel spa', 'The Grand Hyatt''s own spa, on the hotel''s garden level in Yongsan-gu.', null, 'a hotel spa treatment away from street level', 'The Spa occupies the garden level of the Grand Hyatt Seoul, at 322 Sowol-ro in Yongsan-gu, about five minutes'' drive from the Itaewon shopping district. It opened in April 2007.

Treatments are taken in spa suites and treatment rooms, and the menu runs to massages, facials, body treatments, scrubs and wraps.

It is a separate operation from Club Olympus, the hotel''s fitness centre, which has its own men''s and women''s saunas with a Korean body-scrub service, plus indoor, outdoor and children''s pools. Published opening hours differ between sources, so confirm them rather than planning a day around them.', 4.6, 53, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The%20Spa%20Grand%20Hyatt%20Seoul%20Itaewon%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%8D%94%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%20%EA%B7%B8%EB%9E%9C%EB%93%9C%20%ED%95%98%EC%96%8F%ED%8A%B8%20%EC%84%9C%EC%9A%B8', true),
('spa-1899-donginbi', 'Spa 1899 Donginbi', '스파 1899 동인비', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangnam', '서울 강남구 영동대로 416 KT&G 타워 B2층', 'Ginseng spa', 'Red-ginseng spa run by the Donginbi skincare brand, two levels beneath KT&G Tower in Gangnam.', 'The ginseng is not a theme laid over a generic menu. The spa belongs to Donginbi, the skincare line that grew out of the Cheong Kwan Jang red-ginseng business, and its signature course is built on the same material.', 'a red-ginseng treatment course near Samseong Station', 'Spa 1899 is on the second basement level of KT&G Tower, at 416 Yeongdong-daero in Gangnam-gu, about nine minutes on foot from Exit 2 of Samseong Station on Line 2.

It is run by Donginbi, the skincare line that grew out of the Cheong Kwan Jang red-ginseng business, and its treatments are built on that red ginseng. The signature course, Red Ginseng Energy Circulation Therapy, is the spa''s own. Around it sit single-focus programmes of an hour each — facial, body or foot — multi-care courses of two to two and a half hours, and a three-hour full peeling.

Parking is free for guests. Published opening hours differ between the operator''s own page and the tourism listing, so confirm the last appointment when you book.', 4.6, 25, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Spa%201899%20Donginbi%20Gangnam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%201899%20%EB%8F%99%EC%9D%B8%EB%B9%84', true),
('asuca', 'Asuca', 'Asuca', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 중구 장충단로 213', 'Spa', 'Spa listed on Jangchungdan-ro in Jung-gu, with almost nothing published about it.', null, 'confirming what is offered before booking', 'Asuca is listed as a spa at 213 Jangchungdan-ro, in Jung-gu near Dongdaemun.

Beyond the name and the address we found nothing published about it — no operator page, no treatment menu, no tourism or trade listing, in Korean or in English. With no way to establish what the business offers, the entry stays unverified and is not published in the directory.', 4.6, 10, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Asuca%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Asuca', false),
('hera', 'Hera Este', '헤라', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 명동8가길 37, 3~5층', 'Skincare salon', 'Licensed skincare salon across three floors at 37 Myeongdong 8na-gil, two minutes from Myeongdong Station.', 'Every course is published as an ordered list of steps rather than a name and a price, so you can see what a course consists of before you book.', 'a korgi or hydration facial in Myeongdong', 'Hera Este occupies the third, fourth and fifth floors at 37 Myeongdong 8na-gil, in Jung-gu, about two minutes from Exit 10 of Myeongdong Station. Jung-gu''s register of licensed beauty businesses records it there as a skincare premises. Map listings sometimes place it at the neighbouring number, 39, where the register records no beauty business at all.

The menu is short, and each course is published as an ordered sequence rather than a name. The facial line runs from a hydration course — scalp work, cleanse and deep cleanse, facial and neck lymph drainage, a hyaluronic mask — to a korgi course that swaps the cleansing steps for bone-pressing work on the face. Longer courses add a foot spa, exfoliation, a vitamin or gold pack and leg drainage; body courses cover the back, the feet and the whole body.

It is worked by a single practitioner, a licensed esthetician of fifteen years. Published opening hours differ between listings, so confirm the time when you book.', 4.5, 12, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%ED%97%A4%EB%9D%BC%EC%97%90%EC%8A%A4%ED%85%8C%20%EB%AA%85%EB%8F%998%EA%B0%80%EA%B8%B8%2037', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%ED%97%A4%EB%9D%BC%EC%97%90%EC%8A%A4%ED%85%8C', true),
('bamboo-therapy', 'Bamboo Therapy', '뱀부테라피', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Hapjeong', '서울 마포구 양화로18안길 22', 'Foot & body massage', 'Foot-and-body massage shop in Hapjeong whose current operation we could not confirm.', null, 'confirming by phone before you go', 'Bamboo Therapy is listed as a foot-and-body massage shop at 22 Yanghwa-ro 18an-gil, in the Hapjeong area of Mapo-gu.

We could not establish whether it still trades. There is no operator page, no current Korean-language business listing that matches the address, and the material still online about it is several years old.

The entry stays unverified on that basis and is not published in the directory. Do not plan a visit around it without confirming first that it is open.', 4.4, 12, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bamboo%20Therapy%20Hapjeong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%B1%80%EB%B6%80%ED%85%8C%EB%9D%BC%ED%94%BC', false),
('mizo-esthe-salon', 'MIZO Esthe Salon', '미조 에스떼 살롱', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 충무로2가 66-9', 'Esthetic salon', 'Myeongdong esthetic salon built around korgi facial work, a couple of minutes from the station.', 'Its facial work is built on korgi, the Korean bone-pressing massage, and can be taken on its own or paired with a body course.', 'a korgi facial or a body course near Myeongdong Station', 'MIZO Esthe Salon is at 66-9 Chungmuro 2-ga, in Jung-gu, a couple of minutes from Exit 6 of Myeongdong Station on Line 4.

The menu covers more than facial work. The facial course is built on korgi, the Korean bone-pressing massage, and finishes with a pack; alongside it sit full-body massage, a back detox with a hot pack, foot massage and reflexology, air massage and a paraffin pack. Korgi can be booked on its own or with body work added. Couple rooms are available, and the salon takes cards.

The salon''s own web address no longer resolves, and it does not appear on Jung-gu''s register of licensed beauty businesses, so travel listings are the only published source for its details — and they do not agree. The floor is given as both the fourth and the eighth, and the closing time as anywhere from 22:00 to midnight. Bookings run through Japanese travel agencies as well as directly. Confirm the floor, the hours and the price when you reserve.', 4.3, 25, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=MIZO%20Esthe%20Salon%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EB%AF%B8%EC%A1%B0%20%EC%97%90%EC%8A%A4%EB%96%BC%20%EC%82%B4%EB%A1%B1', true),
('seoulistique-skin', 'Seoulistique Skin', 'Seoulistique Skin', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gongdeok', '서울 마포구 마포대로 225', 'Skincare studio', 'K-beauty skincare studio at Aeogae Station, booked by message rather than through a site.', null, 'a non-invasive facial near Aeogae Station', 'Seoulistique Skin is a skincare studio in Mapo-gu, at Exit 2 of Aeogae Station.

It describes its own work narrowly: non-invasive K-beauty skincare treatments. The studio previously traded as Fleur Jardin, and that account now points to this one.

There is no website, no published menu and no price list. Booking is by Instagram message or WhatsApp, and no opening hours are published, so agree a time when you book.', 4.3, 10, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Seoulistique%20Skin%20Gongdeok%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Seoulistique%20Skin', true),
('sulwhasoo-spa', 'Sulwhasoo Spa (Lotte Hotel Seoul)', '설화수 스파', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Euljiro', '서울 중구 을지로 30, 롯데호텔 서울 본관 7층', 'Hotel spa', 'Amorepacific''s Sulwhasoo spa, on the seventh floor of the Lotte Hotel Seoul main building in Jung-gu.', 'Each facial is worked with its own hand-held massager — nephrite jade, white porcelain, amber — rather than one tool used across the menu.', 'a ginseng-based facial course in central Jung-gu', 'Sulwhasoo Spa occupies the seventh floor of the main building of Lotte Hotel Seoul, at 30 Euljiro in Jung-gu. It is not the brand''s flagship-store spa in Gangnam, which is a separate operation at 18 Dosan-daero 45-gil. This one moved up from the hotel''s third and fourth floors and reopened on 1 October 2018 after a redesign.

The menu splits three ways. Facials run from the Moisturizing & Comforting and Calming & Vitalizing treatments through to the Signature Ginseng and The Ultimate S, at 80 to 90 minutes each; body care comes in recovery, circulation and intensive forms of 50 to 90 minutes; and the journeys pair a facial with body work over 100 to 180 minutes.

It opens 10:30 to 21:00 daily, closing on the first Monday of each month and on Seollal and Chuseok. The hotel is being rebranded as The Grand Lotte Seoul, so confirm the spa''s arrangements when you book.', 4.1, 15, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sulwhasoo%20Spa%20Euljiro%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%84%A4%ED%99%94%EC%88%98%20%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C', true),
('individuel-geneve', 'Inko Seoul (formerly Individuel Genève)', 'Individuel Geneve', 'facial'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gangnam', '서울 강남구 봉은사로47길 60', 'Facial & body treatments', 'Skin-analysis-led facial studio near Gangnam-gu Office Station, now trading as Inko Seoul.', 'The course is built from a digital skin scan read across six measures, and the scan is repeated as treatment progresses rather than taken once at the door.', 'a facial assembled from a digital skin analysis', 'Individuel Genève now trades as Inko Seoul. The studio is at 60 Bongeunsa-ro 47-gil in Gangnam-gu, about 600 metres from Exit 2 of Gangnam-gu Office Station; the old web address redirects to the new one, and the KakaoTalk booking channel still runs under the Individuel name.

The method starts with measurement. A digital analyser reads the skin across six points — type, oiliness, pores, spots, wrinkles and impurities — the treatment is assembled from what it returns, and the skin is scanned again as the course runs so the plan can be adjusted.

What gets assembled draws on a published set of technologies: dual-wave ultrasound, magnetic infusion, microneedling with skin boosters, cold plasma, ear seeds, air-therapy lymphatic drainage and LED, worked with active formulas including exosome, NAD+, PDRN, vitamin C and azelaic acid. Colour analysis is offered separately.

No opening hours are published. Booking goes through the site''s form, WhatsApp or KakaoTalk.', 3.9, 37, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Individuel%20Geneve%20Gangnam%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Individuel%20Geneve', true),
('gold-spa', 'Gold Spa', '황금스파', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Dongdaemun', '서울 중구 청계천로 400 롯데캐슬 B2층', 'Jjimjilbang & sauna', 'Jjimjilbang two levels beneath the Lotte Castle Benecia complex on Cheonggyecheon-ro, open around the clock.', null, 'a communal bathhouse rather than a private treatment room', 'Gold Spa is on the second basement level of the Lotte Castle Benecia complex, at 400 Cheonggyecheon-ro in the Hwanghak-dong part of Jung-gu — the same block as a supermarket and a cinema.

It is a jjimjilbang rather than a private spa: the communal bathhouse format, shared bathing and heated rooms rather than a treatment table booked in your name. A restaurant and a shop sit on the same floor, along with a doctor-fish tank charged separately.

It runs 24 hours a day, year round, priced as a day rate and a night rate rather than by the hour, and it does not take reservations — you pay at the desk on arrival. Parking under the building comes with four hours free.', 3.9, 14, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gold%20Spa%20Dongdaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%ED%99%A9%EA%B8%88%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C', true),
('supsok-hanbang-land', 'Supsok Hanbang Land', '숲속 한방 랜드', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Seodaemun', '서울 서대문구 봉원사길 75-7', 'Charcoal kiln sauna', 'Oak-charcoal kiln bathhouse at the foot of Ansan, reached by bus from Sinchon.', 'A charcoal kiln is a different heat from a jjimjilbang''s heated room. The kilns here are held at low, medium and high temperatures, so you work through them in stages rather than picking one and staying in it.', 'the charcoal-kiln version of a Korean sauna', 'Supsok Hanbang Land is at 75-7 Bongwonsa-gil, in Bongwon-dong, on the Seodaemun side of Ansan and next to Bongwonsa temple.

The format is the charcoal kiln rather than the jjimjilbang: domed kilns fired with oak charcoal and held at low, medium and high temperatures. Men''s and women''s bathhouses are separate. There is a restaurant on site, and a fire pit at the kilns where sweet potatoes and rice cakes are roasted.

The grounds open at 06:30 and close at 22:00; the kilns themselves run from 08:00 to 21:00. Getting there means a bus — Sinchon Station on Line 2, then the bus towards Bongwonsa — and the Ansan trails start from the same spot.', 3.9, 11, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Supsok%20Hanbang%20Land%20Seodaemun%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%88%B2%EC%86%8D%20%ED%95%9C%EB%B0%A9%20%EB%9E%9C%EB%93%9C', true),
('sparex-sauna', 'SPAREX Sauna (Dongmyo)', '스파렉스 사우나', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 지봉로 19 시즌빌딩 12층', 'Sauna & jjimjilbang', 'The Sparex chain''s Dongmyo branch — open 24 hours, directly outside Dongmyoap Station Exit 6.', null, 'a 24-hour sauna next to a subway exit', 'This is the Dongmyo branch of Sparex, in the Season Building at 19 Jibong-ro, Changsin-dong, in Jongno-gu. It is not the chain''s Good Morning City branch, which is a separate site at 247 Jangchungdan-ro in Jung-gu, by Dongdaemun History & Culture Park Station.

The Dongmyo branch is open 24 hours, year round, and stands directly outside Exit 6 of Dongmyoap Station, where Lines 1 and 6 meet. Inside are wet and dry saunas, a food court, sleeping areas, and a body-scrub service running day and night. The fit-out is modern — white surfaces and wood — rather than the traditional hanok-style interior the Good Morning City branch is known for.

Luggage storage is available, which makes it usable on a travel day.', 3.6, 65, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sparex%20Sauna%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%EB%A0%89%EC%8A%A4%20%EC%82%AC%EC%9A%B0%EB%82%98', true),
('riverside-spa-land', 'Riverside Spa Land', '강변스파랜드', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Gwangjin', '서울 광진구 구의강변로 45 성진빌딩 지하2층', 'Bulhanjeungmak bathhouse', 'Traditional pine-fired kiln bathhouse over two basement levels in Gwangjin.', 'The main heat source is a pine-log fire rather than an element — the older bulhanjeungmak method — and the rooms around it are graded by material as much as by temperature: charcoal, salt, ochre, silver.', 'the wood-fired end of Korean sauna culture', 'Riverside Spa Land occupies two basement levels at 45 Guui-gangbyeon-ro in Gwangjin-gu, about 9,900 square metres in all.

The centrepiece is a traditional bulhanjeungmak, a kiln heated by burning pine logs rather than by an element. Around it are rooms graded by material: charcoal, salt, a silver pyramid room, ochre rooms, an igloo room, and an ochre kiln reserved for women. The wet side has hot and cold pools, a massage pool, an aqua-walking pool and both wet and dry saunas, drawn on sulphur groundwater.

It is open around the clock, year round, with admission split into a daytime and a night rate. Game rooms, a children''s play area and food service sit alongside the bathing floors.', 3.4, 17, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Riverside%20Spa%20Land%20Gwangjin%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EA%B0%95%EB%B3%80%EC%8A%A4%ED%8C%8C%EB%9E%9C%EB%93%9C', true),
('hokutosichisei', 'Hokutosichisei', '호쿠토시치세이', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Euljiro', '서울 중구 을지로 78 남광빌딩 406호', 'Massage', 'Massage business listed on the fourth floor of an Euljiro office building, with nothing published about it.', null, 'confirming what is offered before booking', 'Hokutosichisei is listed at 78 Euljiro, room 406 of the Namgwang Building, in Jung-gu.

We could find nothing published about it in Korean or English — no operator page, no treatment menu, no tourism or trade listing. With no way to establish what the business offers, the entry stays unverified and is not published in the directory.', 3.4, 12, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hokutosichisei%20Euljiro%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%ED%98%B8%EC%BF%A0%ED%86%A0%EC%8B%9C%EC%B9%98%EC%84%B8%EC%9D%B4', false),
('o2-body-foot', 'O2 Body & Foot', '오투', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 남대문로 78', 'Foot massage', 'Foot-massage shop at 78 Namdaemun-ro in Jung-gu.', null, 'a walk-in foot massage in central Jung-gu', 'O2 is a foot-massage shop at 78 Namdaemun-ro, in Jung-gu. We found no operator page, price list or treatment menu published for it, and no opening hours.

The entry is kept for the record and is not published in the directory.', 2.7, 13, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=O2%20Body%20%26%20Foot%20Myeongdong%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/%EC%98%A4%ED%88%AC', false),
('eco-jardin', 'Eco Jardin (Gyeongbokgung)', 'Eco Jardin', 'head_spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Jongno', '서울 종로구 자하문로 9, 5층', 'Head spa & hair salon', 'The Eco Jardin group''s Jongno branch, at 9 Jahamun-ro near Gyeongbokgung.', null, 'confirming what is offered before booking', 'This is the Jongno branch of Eco Jardin, at 9 Jahamun-ro in Jongno-gu, near Gyeongbokgung. It is a separate premises from the group''s Aeogae branch at 204 Mapo-daero in Mapo-gu. Korean company records list it as a beauty business registered in January 2025, under a different operator from the Aeogae one. Published floor numbers for it disagree.

The entry is kept for the record and is not published in the directory.', 2.6, 10, null, null, 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Eco%20Jardin%20Jongno%20Seoul', 'https://map.naver.com/p/search/Eco%20Jardin', false),
('hwangjok-massage', 'Hwangjok Massage', '황족마사지', 'spa'::place_category, 'place'::place_entry_type, 'Myeongdong', '서울 중구 명동8나길 12 롯데리아 5층', 'Foot & body massage', 'Foot, body and aroma treatments on the fifth floor above a Lotteria in Myeongdong.', null, 'a walk-in massage in Myeongdong', 'Hwangjok Massage is on the fifth floor at 12 Myeongdong 8na-gil, above a Lotteria, in Jung-gu. Korean business listings record it under massage and acupressure, and describe its work as foot, abdominal, full-body and aroma treatment. No opening hours are published.

